# A pile of cards
// A game's stock, its discards, a column on the table:  the game gives each pile its id, and says what each kind takes.
// Each pile is its own element around its cards' elements, `<games-pile>` around `<games-card>`s.
// A card dragged over it glows when it would take the card, by its own rules (`droppable`).

a "pile" is a viewable, droppable list of cards
	its "layout" is one of stacked, vertical, horizontal or fanned
		// How its cards lie:  on top of each other, down a column, along a row, or fanned as a hand is held -- styles.css
	its "color" is
		// Its last card's:  what the next card goes on
		"none" if it is empty
		the color of its last card otherwise
	its "value" is
		// Its last card's
		0 if it is empty
		the value of its last card otherwise
	its "short name" is
		// Its id, then its cards' short names:  stock: Q♠↑ 7♥↓
		set summary to its id + ":"
		for card in the pile
			set summary to summary + " " + the short name of the card
		return summary

	to test piles
		set the stock to a new pile with id "stock"
		the stock's color should be "none"
		the stock's value should be 0
		add (a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is up) to the stock
		add (a new card whose rank is 7, suit is hearts and direction is down) to the stock
		the stock's color should be red
		the stock's value should be 7
		the stock's short name should be "stock: Q♠↑ 7♥↓"

		// a card is in one pile at a time
		set the discards to a new pile with id "discards"
		get the last card of the stock
		add it to the discards
		its pile is the discards should be yes
		the number of cards in the stock should be 1
		the discards' short name should be "discards: 7♥↓"

a card belongs to one pile
	// a card is in one pile at a time:  moving it to another pile takes it off this one
